  {
    "surah_number": 25,
    "asbab_nuzul": "\n (And those who cry not unto any other god along with  Allahà) [25:68-70]. Abu Ishaq al-Thaæalibi informed \nus> al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Makhladi> al-MuÆammil ibn al-Hasan ibn æIsa> al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah al-Zaæfarani> Hajjaj> Ibn Jurayj> Yaæla ibn Mu slim> Saæid ibn Jubayr> Ibn æAbbas who said: ôSome \nidolaters who had committed many murders and fornicated numerous times went to the Messenger of Allah, \nAllah bless him and give him peace, and said: æWhat yo u say and call for is good, if only you could inform us \nwhether there is any expiation for the things we have  committedÆ. As a response, this verse was revealed \n(And those who cry not unto any other god along with  Allah) up to His words (Allah is ever Forgiving, \nMerciful) [25:70]ö. This was narrated by Muslim> Ibrahim ibn Dinar> Hajjaj. Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn \nYahya al-Muzakki informed us> his father> Muhamm ad ibn Ishaq al-Thaqafi> Ibrahim al-Hanzali and \nMuhammad ibn al-Sabbah> Jarir> Mansur and al-Aæmas h> Abu WaÆil> æAmr ibn Shurahbil> Abu Maysarah> \næAbd Allah ibn Masæud who said: ôI asked the Messenger of Allah, Allah bless him and give him peace: æWhat \nis the greatest sin?Æ He said: æIt is to ascribe an equa l to Allah when it is Him Who has created youÆ. I asked: \næWhat comes after that?Æ he said: æIt is to kill your child for fear that he might compete with you over foodÆ. I \nasked: æWhat comes after that?Æ he said: æIt is to comm it adultery with the wife of your neighbourÆ. Allah, \nexalted is He, then revealed these verses to confirm his answers (And those who cry not unto any other god 123 along with Allah, nor take the life which Allah hath  forbidden save in (course of) justice, nor commit \nadulteryà)ö. This was narrated by Bukhari> Musa ddid> Yahya and also by Muslim> æUthman ibn Abi \nShaybah> Jarir. Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith informed us> æAbd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Jaæfar> Ahmad ibn \nMuhammad ibn Ibrahim> Ismaæil ibn Ishaq> al-Harut h ibn al-Zubayr> Abu Rashid, the client of al-\nLahibiyyin> Saæid ibn Salim al-Qaddah> Ibn Jurayh> æAtaÆ> Ibn æAbbas who said: ôWahshiyy went to the \nMessenger of Allah, Allah bless him and give him peac e, and said: æI came to you seeking sanctuary; so \ngrant me sanctuary in order that I can hear the speec h of AllahÆ. The Messenger of Allah, Allah bless him \nand give him peace, said to him: æI had wished to see you without sanctuary, but since you have asked me \nfor sanctuary, you are in my sanctuary until you hear th e speech of AllahÆ. Wahshiyy said: æI have associated \nothers with Allah, killed souls which Allah, exalted is  He, has made forbidden and committed adultery. Does \nAllah accept my repentance?Æ The Messenger of Allah, exalted is He, did not answer him and then the verse \n(And those who cry not unto any other god along with Allah, nor take the life wh ich Allah hath forbidden \nsave in (course of) justice, nor commit adulteryà) was revealed. The Prophet recited it to Wahshiyy but the latter said: æI see here a condition; it is possible that  I may not do any righteous works. I will stay in your \nsanctuary so that I can hear the speech of Allah, exalte d is HeÆ. The verse: (Lo! Allah forgiveth not that a \npartner should be ascribed unto Him. He forgiveth (all) save that to whom He will) [4:48] was then revealed. \nWahshiyy was summoned and the verse was recited to him.  He said: æI could be among (save that to whom \nHe will). I will remain in your sanctuary so that I can hear the speech of AllahÆ. The verse (Say: O My slaves \nwho have been prodigal to their own hurt! Despair no t of the mercy of Allahà) [39:53] was then revealed, \nupon which Wahshiyy said: æYes, now I do not see any conditionsÆ, and so he embraced Islamö.  \n \n",
    "verse_number": 68,
    "surah_englishName": "Al-Furqaan",
    "surah_englishNameTranslation": "The Criterion",
    "reference": "Asbāb al-Nuzūl",
    "book_author": "Alī ibn Ahmad al-Wāhidī"
  },
