  {
    "surah_number": 38,
    "asbab_nuzul": "\n(Maketh he the gods One God? Lo! that is an astoun ding thingà) [38:5-11]. AbuÆl-Qasim ibn Abi Nasr al-\nKhuzaæi informed us> Muhammad ibn æAbd Allah ibn Hamdawayh> Abu Bakr ibn Abi Darim al-Hafiz> \nMuhammad ibn æUthman in Abi Shaybah> his fath er> Muhammad ibn æAbd Allah al-Asdi> Sufyan> al-\nAæmash> Yahya ibn æUmarah> Saæid ibn Jubayr> Ibn æA bbas who said: ôWhen Abu Talib fell ill, the Quraysh \nand the Prophet, Allah bless him and give him peace, went  to visit him. There was, close to the head of Abu \nTalib, enough room for one man to sit, so Abu Jahl rush ed to it to prevent the Prophet from sitting there. \nThey complained to Abu Talib about the Prophet. Abu Talib  said to the Prophet: æSon of my brother, what is \nit that you want from your own people?Æ He said: æO uncle, I want from them one word by means of which \nall the Arabs will surrender to them and all the non-Ar abs will pay exemption tax to themÆ. æWhat is this \nword?Æ he asked. He said: æThere is no deity except AllahÆ. They all exclaimed: æDoes he make the gods One \nGod?Æ The QurÆan was then revealed about them (S ad. By the renowned QurÆan, nay, but those who \ndisbelieve are in false pride and schismà) up to AllahÆ s words (This is naught but an invention) [38:1-7]ö. \nThe commentators of the QurÆan said: ôWhen æUmar ibn al-Khattab embraced Islam, the Muslims were \noverjoyed while the Quraysh was devastated. Al-Walid ibn al-Mughirah said to the nobles and chiefs of \nQuraysh: æGo to Abu Talib and say to him: you are ou r elder and chief and you know well what these fools \nhave done. We have come to you so that you judge between us and your nephewÆ. Abu Talib sent for the \nProphet, Allah bless him and give him peace, and when he answered his call, he said to him: æSon of my \nbrother, these are your own people and they are asking  you for fairness, so do not swerve completely from \nthemÆ. The Prophet asked: æWhat do they want from me ?Æ They said: æCease mentioning our deities and we \nwill leave you alone with your GodÆ. The Prophet, Allah bless him and give him peace, said to them: æWill you \ngrant me one word by means of which you will rule over the Arabs and subjugate the non-Arabs?Æ Abu Jahl said: æWe will surely grant it and grant you ten like it!Æ  The Prophet, Allah bless him and give him peace, \nsaid: æSay: there is no deity except Allah!Æ The Qurays h were repelled and left, saying: æDoes he make the \ngods One God? How can One God be sufficient for the whol e creation?Æ And so Allah, exalted is He, revealed \nabout them these verses, up to His words (The folk of Noah before them denied (their messenger)à) [38:12]ö.   ",
    "verse_number": 5,
    "surah_englishName": "Saad",
    "surah_englishNameTranslation": "The letter Saad",
    "reference": "Asbāb al-Nuzūl",
    "book_author": "Alī ibn Ahmad al-Wāhidī"
  },
