  {
    "surah_number": 107,
    "asbab_nuzul": "\n (Hast thou observed him who belieth religion? That is he who repelleth the orphan) [107:1-2]. Muqatil and al-Kalbi said: ôThis Surah was revealed about al-æAs ib n WaÆil al-Sahmiö. And Ibn Jurayj said: ôAbu Sufyan ibn \nHarb was in the habit of slaughtering two camels every week. On one occasion, an orphan came to him \nasking him for something. Abu Sufyan responded by hitting  him with a stick. And so Allah, exalted is He, \nrevealed (Hast thou observed him who belieth relig ion? That is he who repelleth the orphan)ö.  \n  \n(Al-Kawthar)  \n \n",
    "verse_number": 1,
    "surah_englishName": "Al-Maa'un",
    "surah_englishNameTranslation": "Almsgiving",
    "reference": "Asbāb al-Nuzūl",
    "book_author": "Alī ibn Ahmad al-Wāhidī"
  },
