  {
    "surah_number": 64,
    "verse_number": 14,
    "asbab_nuzul": "\n (O ye who believe! Lo! among your wives and your child ren there are enemies for you, therefor beware of \nthem. And if ye efface and overlook and forgive, then  lo! Allah is Forgiving, Merciful) [64:14]. Said Ibn \næAbbas: ôSome men used to embrace Islam but, upon tr ying to migrate, were prevented from doing so by \ntheir families and children. The latter would plead with them, saying: æWe plead with you, by Allah, not to \nleave your family and clan and depart to Medina wher e you have no family or wealthÆ. Some of these men \ntook pity on their family and children and stayed back, thus failing to migrate, and so Allah, exalted is He, \nrevealed this verseö. Ahmad ibn æAbd Allah ibn Ahma d al-Shaybani informed us> AbuÆl-Fadl Ahmad ibn \nIsmaæil ibn Yahya ibn Hazim> æUmar ibn Muhammad ibn Bujayr> Muhammad ibn æU mar al-Maqdimi> Ashæath \nibn æAbd Allah> Shuæbah> Ismaæil ibn Abi Khalid who sa id: ôSome men used to embrace Islam but then faced \nthe rebuke of their families and children, and so this verse was revealed (O ye who believe! Lo! among your \nwives and your children there are enemies for you, therefor beware of themà)ö. Reporting from Ibn æAbbas, æIkrimah said: ôThis refers to those who were prevente d by their families from emigrating to Medina. When \nthey finally migrated and saw that people had gained a clear understanding of the religion, they were about \nto punish those members of their family who prevented them from migrating, and so Allah, exalted is He, \nrevealed (And if ye efface and overlook and fo rgive, then lo! Allah is Forgiving, Merciful)ö.  \n  \n(At-TalΓq)  \n \n",
    "surah_englishName": "At-Taghaabun",
    "surah_englishNameTranslation": "Mutual Disillusion",
    "reference": "Asbāb al-Nuzūl",
    "book_author": "Alī ibn Ahmad al-Wāhidī"
  },
  {
    "surah_number": 65,
    "verse_number": 1,
    "asbab_nuzul": "\n (O Prophet! When ye (men) put away women, put th em away for their (legal) periodà) [65:1]. Qatadah \nreported that Anas said: ôThe Messenger of Allah, Al lah bless him and give him peace, divorced Hafsah and \nso Allah, exalted is, revealed this verse. It was said  to him: æTake her back, for she is one who fasts often \nand stands up in night vigil prayerÆ often, and she is on e of your wives in the GardenÆ ö. Al-Suddi said: ôThis \nverse was revealed about æAbd Allah ibn æUmar who di vorced his wife while she was in her menses. The \nMessenger of Allah, Allah bless him and give him peace,  ordered him to take her back and keep her until the \nperiod of her menses was over and then wait again until she was in her menses. When she became pure, he \nwas free to divorce her provided that he did not sleep with her before that, for th is was the waiting period \nwhich Allah has commanded to observeö. Mansur ibn æAbd al-Wahhab ibn Ahmad al-Shalanji> Abu æAmr \nMuhammad ibn Ahmad al-Hiri> Muhammad ibn Zanjaway h> æAbd al-æAziz ibn Yahya> al-Layth ibn Saæd> \nNafiæ> Ibn æUmar who divorced his wife one single divorce while she was still in her menses. The Messenger of Allah, Allah bless him and give him peace, comman ded him to keep her until the period of her menses \nwas over. He had then to wait until she was in her peri od, and if he was still determined to divorce, he had \nto wait until her period was over, provided that he did not sleep with her before divorcing her. This was the \nwaiting period in which Allah, exalted is He, has or dered that women be divorced. This was narrated by \nBukhari and Muslim from Qutaybah and al-Layth respectively.  \n ",
    "surah_englishName": "At-Talaaq",
    "surah_englishNameTranslation": "Divorce",
    "reference": "Asbāb al-Nuzūl",
    "book_author": "Alī ibn Ahmad al-Wāhidī"
  },
  {
    "surah_number": 65,
    "verse_number": 3,
    "asbab_nuzul": "\n (And whosoever keepeth his duty to Allah, Allah will a ppoint a way out for him, And will provide for him from \n(a quarter) whence he hath no expectation) [65:3]. This verse was revealed about 'Awf ibn Malik al-Ashja'i \nwhose son was imprisoned by the idolaters. He went to  the Messenger of Allah, Allah bless him and give him \npeace, and complained to him about his poverty, sayi ng: ôThe enemy has imprisoned my son and his mother \nis very distressed, what do you advise me to do?ö The Prophet, Allah bless him and give him peace, said to \nhim: ôBe fearful of Allah and be patient. I also comma nd you and your wife to often repeat 'there is no \nstrength or might except by Allah' ö. So he went home  and said to his wife: ôThe Messenger of Allah, Allah \nbless him and give him peace, commanded both of us to often repeat 'there is no strength or might except \nby Allah' ö. She said: ôHow good is that with which he has commanded us!ö And they both started saying it \nstraightaway. It happened that the enemy became distra cted from their son and the latter led their sheep 158 away and fled. He brought these sheep to his father ; they were four thousand heads. This verse was \nrevealed about this incident. 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Abda n informed us> Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Nu'aym> \nAbu'l-Qasim al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al -Sakuni> 'Ubayd ibn Kathir al-'Amiri> 'Abbad ibn \nYa'qub> Yahya ibn Adam> Isra'il> 'Ammar ibn Mu'awiya h> Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd> Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah who \nsaid: ôThis verse (And whosoever keepeth his duty to Allah, Allah will appoint a way out for him, And will \nprovide for him from (a quarter) whence he hath no  expectation) was revealed about a man from Ashja'. \nThis man was poor but had numerous children. He went to the Messenger of Allah, Allah bless him and give \nhim peace, and asked him for help. The Prophet, Allah bless him and give him peace, told him: 'Fear Allah \nand be patient!' The man went back to his companio ns and when they asked him about what the Prophet \nhad given him, he said: 'He did not give me anything; he simply said: Fear Allah and be patient'. Not long \nafter this, a son of this man, who had been captured  by the enemy, brought him sheep. The man went to \nthe Messenger of Allah, Allah bless him and give him pe ace, to ask him about what he should do with the \nsheep, and told him the full story. The Messenger of Alla h, Allah bless him and give him peace, said to him: \n'Keep them, they are yours' ö.  \n",
    "surah_englishName": "At-Talaaq",
    "surah_englishNameTranslation": "Divorce",
    "reference": "Asbāb al-Nuzūl",
    "book_author": "Alī ibn Ahmad al-Wāhidī"
  },
  {
    "surah_number": 65,
    "verse_number": 4,
    "asbab_nuzul": "\n (And for such of your women as despair of menstrua tionà) [65:4]. Said Muqatil: ôWhen the verse (Women \nwho are divorced shall wait, keeping themselves apartà ), Kallad ibn al-Nuæman ibn Qays al-Ansari said: æO \nMessenger of Allah, what is the waiting period of the woman who does not menstruate and the woman who \nhas not menstruated yet? And what is the waiting period  of the pregnant woman?Æ And so Allah, exalted is \nHe, revealed this verseö. Abu Ishaq al-MuqriÆ info rmed us> Muhammad ibn æAbd Allah ibn Hamdun> Makki \nibn æAbdan> AbuÆl-Azhar> Asbat ibn Muhammad> Muta rrif> Abu æUthman æAmr ibn Salim who said: ôWhen \nthe waiting period for divorced and widowed women was mentioned in Surah al-Baqarah, Ubayy ibn Kaæb \nsaid: æO Messenger of Allah, some women of Medina are saying: there are other women who have not been \nmentioned!Æ He asked him: æAnd who are they?Æ He said : æThose who are too young [such that they have not \nstarted menstruating yet], those who are too old [whose menstruation has stopped] and those who are \npregnantÆ. And so this verse (And for such of your women as despair of menstruationà) was revealedö.  \n  \n(At-Tahrεm)  \n \n",
    "surah_englishName": "At-Talaaq",
    "surah_englishNameTranslation": "Divorce",
    "reference": "Asbāb al-Nuzūl",
    "book_author": "Alī ibn Ahmad al-Wāhidī"
  },
  {
    "surah_number": 66,
    "verse_number": 1,
    "asbab_nuzul": "\n (O Prophet! Why bannest thou that which Allah hath made lawful for theeà) [66:1]. Muhammad ibn Mansur \nal-Tusi informed us> 'Ali ibn 'Umar ibn Mahdi> al-Hus ayn ibn Isma'il al-Mahamili> 'Abd Allah ibn Shabib> \nIshaq ibn Muhammad> 'Abd Allah ibn 'U mar> Abu'l-Nadr, the client of 'Umar ibn 'Abd Allah> 'Ali ibn 'Abbas> \nIbn 'Abbas> 'Umar who said: ôThe Messenger of Allah,  Allah bless him and give him peace, entered the \nhouse of Hafsah along with the mother of his son, Mar iyah. When Hafsah found him with her [in an intimate \nmoment], she said: 'Why did you bring her in my house?  You did this to me, to the exception of all your \nwives, only because I am too insignificant to you'. He sa id to her: 'Do not mention this to 'A'ishah; she is \nforbidden for me [i.e. Mariyah] if I ever touch her'. Ha fsah said: 'How could she be forbidden for you when \nshe is your slave girl?' He swore to her that he will not touch her and then said: 'Do not mention this \nincident to anyone'. But she went ahead and informed  'A'ishah. The Prophet, Allah bless him and give him \npeace, decided not to go to his wives for a month. He stayed away from them twenty nine days when Allah, \nglorious and exalted is He, revealed (O Prophet! Why bannest thou that which Allah hath made lawful for \nthee, seeking to please thy wives?)ö. Abu Ibrahim Isma 'il ibn Ibrahim al-Wa'iz informed us> Bishr ibn Ahmad \nibn Bishr> Ja'far ibn al-Hasan al-Firyabi> Minjab ib n al-Harith> 'Ali ibn Mushir> Hisham ibn 'Urwah> his \nfather> 'A'ishah who said: ôThe Messenger of Allah, A llah bless him and give him peace, used to like sweet \nand honey. It was also his habit to go to his wives afte r finishing the 'Asr prayer. In one occasion he went to \nHafsah bint 'Umar and stayed with her more than he  usually did. When I found out about this, I enquired \nabout the reason and I was told that a woman from her clan gifted her with a pot of honey which she offered to the Prophet, Allah bless him and give him peace.  I said to myself: by Allah I will spoil it for him. I \nsaid to Sawdah bint Zam'ah: 'When he comes to your apartment and draws closer to you, say: O Messenger \nof Allah, did you eat Maghafir?' When he says: 'Hafsa h fed me some honey', say: 'The bees which produced \nit must have eaten the 'Urfut'. I will say the same th ing, and you, Safiyyah, should say the same'. Sawdah \nsaid: 'By Allah, the moment he stood  at the door I was about to begi n what she commanded me to do'. 159 When he drew closer to her she said: 'O Messenger of  Allah, did you eat Maghafir?' 'No!' he replied. She \nsaid: 'Then, what is this smell on you?' He said: 'H afsah fed me some honey!' she said: ôThe bees which \nproduced it must have eaten the 'Urfut'. When he came  to me, I said the same thing. And when he went to \nSafiyyah she also repeated the same thing. When it was Hafsah's turn and the Prophet went to her, she said \nto him: 'O Messenger of Allah, shall I feed you some of  that honey?' He said: 'I do not feel like it!' Sawdah \nsaid: 'Glory be to Allah, we have deprived him [of honey]'. But I said to  her: 'Be quiet!' ö This was narrated \nby Bukhari from Farwah ibn Abi al-Maghra', and also by Muslim from Suwayd ibn Sa'id ; and both Farwah and Suwayd related it from 'Ali ibn Mushir. Abu 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Hamid informed us> Zahir ibn Ahmad> al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Mus'ab> Yahya ibn Hakim> Abu Dawud> 'Amir al-Khazzaz> Ibn Abi \nMulaykah who related that Sawdah bint Zam'ah had rela tives from her mother's side in the Yemen who used \nto gift her honey. Among all the wives of the Prophe t, Allah bless him and give him peace, Hafsah and \n'A'ishah were very close to each other. One of them sa id to the other: ôDo you no t see this? He goes to her \nwhen it is not her turn just to have some of that ho ney. So when he comes to you hold your nose, and when \nhe asks you about the reason, say: I smell something in you that I do not know what it is. When he comes \nto me, I shall say the same thingö. When the Prophet, Allah bless him and give him peace, went to her she \nheld her nose. He asked her: ôWhat's wrong?ö She said: ôI smell something in you and I think it is the smell \nof Maghafirö. The Messenger of Allah, Allah bless him and give him peace, used to put on him good perfume \nwhenever he found it. When he went to his other wife and she said the same thing. He said: ôSo-and-so said the same thing to me; this must be something that I at e at the house of Sawdah, and, by Allah, I will never \neat it again!ö Ibn Abi Mulaykah reported that Ibn 'Abba s said: ôThe verse (O Prophet! Why bannest thou that \nwhich Allah hath made lawful for thee, seeking to plea se thy wives?) was revealed about this [the incident \nreported above]ö.  \n ",
    "surah_englishName": "At-Tahrim",
    "surah_englishNameTranslation": "The Prohibition",
    "reference": "Asbāb al-Nuzūl",
    "book_author": "Alī ibn Ahmad al-Wāhidī"
  },
  {
    "surah_number": 66,
    "verse_number": 4,
    "asbab_nuzul": "\n (If ye twain turn unto Allah repentant, (ye have cause to  do so) for your hearts desired (the ban)à) [66:4]. \nAbu Mansur al-Mansuri informed us> AbuÆl-Hasan al -Daraqutni> al-Husayn ibn Ismaæil> æAbd Allah ibn \nShabib> Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn æAbd al-æAziz> his fa ther> al-Zuhri> æUbayd Allah ibn æAbd Allah> Ibn \næAbbas who said: ôHafsah found the Messenger of Alla h, Allah bless him and give him peace, with Umm \nIbrahim when it was æAÆishahÆs turn. She said to him: æI will definitely inform her!Æ The Messenger of Allah, \nAllah bless him and give him peace, said: æShe is forb idden for me if I touch her againÆ. Hafsah went ahead \nand informed æAÆishah. Allah informed His Messenger of this and he let Hafsah know some of the things she \nsaid. She asked him: æWho informed you of this?Æ He said: æ(The Knower, the Awar e hath told me) [66:3]Æ. \nThe Messenger of Allah, Allah bless him and give him peace, stayed away from his wives for a month and \nthen Allah, glorious and exalted is He, revealed: (If ye  twain turn unto Allah repentant, (ye have cause to do \nso) for your hearts desired (the ban)à)ö.   ",
    "surah_englishName": "At-Tahrim",
    "surah_englishNameTranslation": "The Prohibition",
    "reference": "Asbāb al-Nuzūl",
    "book_author": "Alī ibn Ahmad al-Wāhidī"
  },
  {
    "surah_number": 67,
    "verse_number": 13,
    "asbab_nuzul": "\n(And keep your opinion secret or proclaim ità) [ 67:13]. Said Ibn æAbbas: ôThis was revealed about the \nidolaters who used to slander the Messenger of Allah, Allah bless him and give him peace. Gabriel, peace be \nupon him, informed him about what they said about him and the things with which they slandered him. Some of them used to say to others: æLower yo ur voices lest MuhammadÆs Allah hears youÆ ö.  \n \n",
    "surah_englishName": "Al-Mulk",
    "surah_englishNameTranslation": "The Sovereignty",
    "reference": "Asbāb al-Nuzūl",
    "book_author": "Alī ibn Ahmad al-Wāhidī"
  },
  {
    "surah_number": 68,
    "verse_number": 4,
    "asbab_nuzul": "\n (And lo! thou art of a tremendous nature) [68:4] . Abu Bakr al-Harithi informed us> æAbd Allah ibn \nMuhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan> Ahmad ibn Jaæfar > ibn Nasr al-Jamal> Jarir ibn Yahya> Husayn ibn \næUlwan al-Kufi> Hisham ibn æUrwah> his father> æAÆish ah who said: ôNo one had a better character than the \nMessenger of Allah, Allah bless him and give him peace. Never did anyone among his Companions, or \nhousehold, call him except that he said: æI am at your se rvice!Æ this is why Allah, glorious and majestic is He, \nrevealed (And lo! thou art of a tremendous nature)ö.   ",
    "surah_englishName": "Al-Qalam",
    "surah_englishNameTranslation": "The Pen",
    "reference": "Asbāb al-Nuzūl",
    "book_author": "Alī ibn Ahmad al-Wāhidī"
  },
  {
    "surah_number": 68,
    "verse_number": 51,
    "asbab_nuzul": "\n (And lo! those who disbelieve would fain disconcert theeà) [68:51]. This verse was revealed when the 160 disbelievers wanted to give the evil eye to the Messenge r of Allah, Allah bless him and give him peace. Some \npeople from the Quraysh looked once at him and sa id: ôWe have never seen anyone like him or like his \nproofsö. The Banu Asad were renowned for their evil ey e. A fat camel or cow would pass by one of them \nand, after giving it the evil eye, he would say to his sl ave-girl: ôO girl, take a large basket and a silver coin \nand bring us some of the meat of this!ö The camel or cow would fall dead straight after that and would then \nbe hamstrung. Said al-Kalbi: ôThere was a man from th e Arabs who used to abstain from food for two or \nthree days and then raise part of his tent, upon the passing by of cattle, and say: æThere are no grazing \ncamels or sheep today better than theseÆ, and the ca ttle would not proceed far before some of them would \nfall dead. The disbelievers requested th is man to give the evil eye to the Messenger of Allah, Allah bless him \nand give him peace, but Allah, exalted is He, pr otected His Prophet and revealed this verseö.  \n ",
    "surah_englishName": "Al-Qalam",
    "surah_englishNameTranslation": "The Pen",
    "reference": "Asbāb al-Nuzūl",
    "book_author": "Alī ibn Ahmad al-Wāhidī"
  },
  {
    "surah_number": 69,
    "verse_number": 12,
    "asbab_nuzul": "\n (àand that remembering ears (that heard the stor y) might remember) [69:12]. Abu Bakr al-Tamimi \ninformed us> æAbd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Jaæfar> al-W alid ibn Abban> al-æAbbas al-Duri> Bishr ibn Adam> \næAbd Allah ibn al-Zubayr> Salih ibn Haytham> Buraydah  who reported that the Messenger of Allah, Allah \nbless him and give him peace, said to æAli: ôAllah ha s commanded me to draw you closer to me and not \nexclude you and that I teach you so that you underst and; and Allah has taken it upon Himself that you \nunderstandö, and then this verse was revealed (and that remembering ears (that heard the story) might remember).   \n(Al-MaæΓrij)  \n \n",
    "surah_englishName": "Al-Haaqqa",
    "surah_englishNameTranslation": "The Reality",
    "reference": "Asbāb al-Nuzūl",
    "book_author": "Alī ibn Ahmad al-Wāhidī"
  },
  {
    "surah_number": 70,
    "verse_number": 1,
    "asbab_nuzul": "\n(A questioner questioned concerning the doom about to  fall) [70:1]. This verse was revealed about al-Nadr \nibn al-Harith when he said [as reported in the QurÆan] (O Allah! if this be indeed the truth from Thee, then \nrain down stones on us or bring on us some painfu l doom!) [8:32], and so he prayed against himself and \nasked for chastisement. He got what he asked for at the Battle of Badr when he was killed in captivity. And \nthe verse (A questioner questioned concerning th e doom about to fall) was revealed about him.  \n \n",
    "surah_englishName": "Al-Ma'aarij",
    "surah_englishNameTranslation": "The Ascending Stairways",
    "reference": "Asbāb al-Nuzūl",
    "book_author": "Alī ibn Ahmad al-Wāhidī"
  },
  {
    "surah_number": 75,
    "verse_number": 3,
    "asbab_nuzul": "\n (Thinketh man that We shall not assemble his bones? ) [75:3]. This verse was revealed about æAdiyy ibn \nRabiæah. The latter went to the Prophet, Allah bless him and give him peace, and said: ôTell me about the \nDay of Arising, when is it going to be? How is it go ing to be?ö The Prophet, Allah bless him and give him \npeace, answered his questions. Then æAdiyy said: ôIf I were to see that Day with my own eyes, I would not \naccept what you say, O Muhammad, as true nor would I believe in yo u. Can Allah really assemble these \nbones?ö And so Allah, exalted is He, revealed this verse.   \n",
    "surah_englishName": "Al-Qiyaama",
    "surah_englishNameTranslation": "The Resurrection",
    "reference": "Asbāb al-Nuzūl",
    "book_author": "Alī ibn Ahmad al-Wāhidī"
  },
